208:    The class XNLP was first introduced by Elberfeld et al.~\cite{ElberfeldST15}, and was renamed
209:    to XNLP in~\cite{BodlaenderGNS22a}. Also, Bodlaender et al.~\cite{BodlaenderGNS22a} introduced
210:    a problem that they named \textsc{NNCCM Acceptance}, and showed it to be XNLP-complete. This problem, defined below, is used as starting point for our reductions.
