692:        It is easy to see that this gives an alternative, equivalent model of the NNCCM. So, we assume we have an accepting run of the NNCCM in this alternative model.
812:\subsection{XNLP-hardness for Trees}
818:        \textsc{Directed Bandwidth} is \textup{XNLP}-complete, even for inputs that are either a downward directed tree or an upward directed tree, with as parameter target value.
822:    Membership follows the same way as the XNLP-membership for DAGs. We now show XNLP-hardness for downward directed trees, and the result for upward directed trees follows directly (just reverse the direction of all arcs).
