+"""Verified Binary Shuffle Product generator for arXiv:2605.03727.
+
+The answer is the bijection in Definition 1 of the paper, represented by one
+increasing list of target positions per source word.  Instances are generated
+inversely: random binary source words are sampled first, then their next
+letters are emitted according to a hidden cyclic shear.  The carried position
+lists are therefore known without solving the resulting shuffle instance.
+"""
